{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1504371-wod-changing-the-events","id":1504371,"title":"WOD changing the events","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-04T09:51:17-08:00","id":1504371,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> WOD changing the events","content":"This crossed my mind while reading the post about GoF. As you are about changing some canonical events in your chronicles, I know that there are people who do this, but I wanted to know how far it is possible or accetable to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T11:50:29-08:00","id":1504377,"title":"","content":"As I see it, the WoD hit the ground solid, but it was difficult to make a business out of a static setting and very easy to make money writing bombastic world shaking plots that fans feel obliged to purchase, so they found a child of seven, asked him to write the most exciting story he could, took that and ran with it. Without going wild for the sake of going wild, There's little you can think up that'll exceeds that bullshittery of nuking the umbra (probably Dr Strangelove style) or having Ravana wake up to destroy india without mortals really noticing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T16:06:27-08:00","id":1504387,"title":"","content":"It's your game, you can change stuff as much or as little as you want. <br /> <br /> I haven't played a Vampire game in almost 20 years that involved ANY of the game's current events or even much of the backstory. I don't even use Generation or have anything for certain existing before the clan founders. All clans are equally part of the Camarilla and Anarchs. My Justicars are structured completely different. And so on. In a similar vein, my Dark Ages games are all set in the mid 12th century, and the power structures being different.<br /> My Mage games have various different or altered subfactions, a total lack of umbral strongholds, and the only current event is the recent fall off Doisetep.<br /> With Wraith, I only have six Legions and a totally different political structure. And so on and on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T16:11:50-08:00","id":1504388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1504371-wod-changing-the-events?p=1504387#post1504387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's your game, you can change stuff as much or as little as you want.<br /> <br /> I haven't played a Vampire game in almost 20 years that involved ANY of the game's current events or even much of the backstory. I don't even use Generation or have anything for certain existing before the clan founders. All clans are equally part of the Camarilla and Anarchs. My Justicars are structured completely different. And so on. In a similar vein, my Dark Ages games are all set in the mid 12th century, and the power structures being different.<br /> My Mage games have various different or altered subfactions, a total lack of umbral strongholds, and the only current event is the recent fall off Doisetep.<br /> With Wraith, I only have six Legions and a totally different political structure. And so on and on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow is refreshing read you answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T09:54:46-08:00","id":1504599,"title":"","content":"Since, rather we like to admit it or not, supernatural politics influence mundane politics I think it would be really be hard to predict something from Rome back for how the modern landscape would look. Personally I wouldn't go any further back then 1230 the start of dark ages to make timeline changes but, I also think that if you want to make changes that you should because the only cannon that matters is the one you set at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T18:05:19-08:00","id":1504681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1504371-wod-changing-the-events?p=1504388#post1504388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somehow is refreshing read you answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will mention that there are threads in several of the forums concerning people's various ideas for alterations to the setting, rules, and other aspects of the games. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1382386-general-headcanons#post1382386\">World of Darkness: General Headcanons</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1357086-headcanons#post1357086\">Vampire: Headcanons</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1357074-head-canons-home-brew#post1357074\">Werewolf: Head Canons &amp; Home Brew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360544-homebrew-headcanons#post1360544\">Mage: Homebrew &amp; Headcanons</a> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T10:02:44-08:00","id":1504768,"title":"","content":"Go as far as you like in changing anything you want. It may be the case that some people may not like it if you make changes from canon, but in my observation, keeping things from older editions never make people mad. If you decided that there were no Tremere in the Camarilla (assuming a Camarilla game) someone might want to play a Tremere and get irritated, but if you said that the Gangrel still existed in the Camarilla, then it's really unlikely that you'd get complaints.<br /> <br /> Personally, I haven't incorporated a significant metaplot change in one of my chronicles since 2nd edition. I didn't even do Revised, much less 5th edition. To take it further, I've made plenty of changes to canon ideas that go all the way back to the first editions, and most people have been alright with it in real life games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T08:54:07-07:00","id":1505317,"title":"","content":"It would be easier to list the things I kept rather than the things I changed. To me metaplot and setting details are just a toolbox to pull from, like rules, and use as I see fit. The game is meant to be your own. Make it so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-27T10:08:08-07:00","id":1506640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1504371-wod-changing-the-events?p=1504768#post1504768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go as far as you like in changing anything you want. It may be the case that some people may not like it if you make changes from canon, but in my observation, keeping things from older editions never make people mad. If you decided that there were no Tremere in the Camarilla (assuming a Camarilla game) someone might want to play a Tremere and get irritated, but if you said that the Gangrel still existed in the Camarilla, then it's really unlikely that you'd get complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, this does definitely seem to be an interesting and also reasonable approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}